8% at Pellham Power and up 12% at Norvane Utilities, mostly substations and transformers (`utility-capex-2027`).\n- **Debt alone isn't filling the gap at Pellham.** Its C$2.4B equity offering was withdrawn after demand fell short. It is now cutting 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and deferring two substation programmes until financing improves (`pellham-offering`). Pellham is the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria. Two utility share offerings were also cut back in size (`utility-credit`).\n- **Norvane looks better placed.** Its bond priced comfortably, so a 12% increase looks fundable with debt.\n\n**Gaps:** I found no data on leverage, credit ratings, debt maturities or total funding needs. I can't say whether Pellham could replace the withdrawn equity with more debt without pressure on its ratings. The sources suggest it chose to cut spending rather than do that.\n\n**Bottom line:** Stronger names like Norvane can likely fund 2027 through debt. Pellham's plan is already being scaled back, and the equity side (n6's question) is the weak link.","ttft_ms":2210,"type":"result","duration_ms":18948,"uuid":"20a8534b-dcfb-4b12-b2f8-b858df408383","ttft_stream_ms":1411,"time_to_request_ms":68,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":6,"system_prompt":4,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":12,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":4,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":5,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":9,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":17,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":68,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":204,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":131,"process_rss_mib_result":203,"process_anon_mib_result":122,"process_peak_rss_mib":222